        package '01 - CubeSat System Reference Model' {
            doc /* Source XMI: _18_0_6_3e4019a_1472151505478_730469_12299
            Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619897478239_980936_70532 (Explanation)
            This package contains the CSRM core. Additoinally, there are links to the examples and illustrations. You are free to use the elements or delete them if they do not apply to your design.
            Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619897531064_593205_70559 (Explanation)
            This package contains CSRM examples and illustrations. This is provided to aid in development and to explain how to use the CSRM.
            Be careful to not use the elements in this package as part of your design. We suggest copying any element to the primary model.
            This section should be removed when not required for reference.
            UML kind: uml:Package */
            package '1 - Stakeholders' {
                doc /* Source XMI: _18_0_6_3e4019a_1472151507121_296228_12349
                Comment _18_4_1_3880181_1494685327661_292254_51026
                Stakeholders are any entities that have an interest or role in the system such as regulatory agencies, the deployer system, and mission system development and operations personnel.  Representative stakeholders are included in the model and can be extended as appropriate.
                There can be a number of stakeholders with varying interests.  Mission needs, objectives, constraints, and Rqts result from review, assessment, and integration of the varied interests.
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619209166835_618099_2322 (HowTo)
                Double-click on on the individual Regulatory Agency Stakeholders to navigate to the stakeholder web sites
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619209166835_732067_2333 (HowTo)
                Double-click on the stakeholder packages to navigate to the individual stakeholders.
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619209166835_759559_2344 (Explanation)
                A stakeholder is any entity that has an interest in the system. Some are interested in the models themselves and others are interested in the missions that can be realized from the mission-specific instantiations of the model, and some have interests in both.
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619209166850_845595_2355 (Explanation)
                There are two modeling efforts. One is the SSWG developing a CubeSat Reference Model with its logical architecture. The other is a team eventually taking the CubeSat Reference Model as a basis for its mission-specific logical and physical architectures.
                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1637431073670_854193_55314 (Explanation)
                Stakeholders
                UML kind: uml:Package */
                package '1.1 Regulatory Agency Stakeholders' {
                    doc /* Source XMI: _18_0_6_3e4019a_1472151555147_792733_13596
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600788576667_236770_63294
                    CubeSat projects are pursued internationally, but the licenses and regulations that cover their activities are administered at the national level. The timelines and procedures for requesting and receiving approval must be well understood and part of the model.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619206846073_966237_942 (Explanation)
                    CubeSat projects are pursued internationally, but the licenses and regulations that cover their activities are administered at the national level. The timelines and procedures for requesting and receiving approval must be well understood and part of the model.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619206846073_430884_964 (Explanation)
                    A double click on these elements links to the web sites
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619206846073_789781_975 (Explanation)
                    A mission specific team will add  Regulatory Agencies as applicable
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619206879285_77215_994 (HowTo)
