            package '4 - Requirements' {
                doc /* Source XMI: _18_0_6_3e4019a_1472151507106_525939_12342
                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600785908876_82097_62844
                The Rqts and logical architecture hierarchies are parallel constructs.
                Requirement packages are numbered to be consistent with the corresponding architecture packages.
                Individual Rqts are numbered uniquely according to a prefix based on the name of the Rqts packages.  The modeler can easily change the prefix.
                The CSRM provides for tracing Rqts from stakeholders, behaviors, and technical measures down to subsystems and components and then to validation and verification activities.
                The requirement element properties include:
                Rationale    Traced To     Traced From    Derived From    Refined By    Verify Method    Verified By    Satisfied By
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619536885345_618868_22192 (Explanation)
                The modeler can easily change the prefix by Select a requirement in the containment tree and Select Element Numbering
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619536885356_427495_22203 (HowTo)
                Double-click on table and add and delete requirements as needed
                Click on Add New to add a new requirement to the containment tree and to the table.
                Right click the new requirement in the table then left click Select in Containment Tree to navigate to the new element.
                Select an requirement and click on Delete to delete from the requirement table and the Containment Tree.
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619536885363_89589_22214 (HowTo)
                Double-click on the CubeSat, Ground Segment, CubeSat Subsystem, and Ground Subsystem requirement packages to navigate to the requirement tables.
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619536885368_134395_22225 (Explanation)
                The requirement element properties include:
                Rationale    Traced To     Traced From    Derived From    Verify Method    Verified By    Satisfied By
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619536885372_64195_22236 (Explanation)
                Requirement packages are numbered to be consistent with the corresponding architecture packages.
                Individual requirements are numbered uniquely according to a prefix based on the name of the requirements packages.
                Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619536885375_539114_22247 (Explanation)
                The requirement elements reside in the containment tree.  The requirement tables are views of the requirement elements.  A table can be deleted but the requirement elements and their hierarchy remains.
                Requirements are added to the table using “Add New or “Add Nested” and the requirement Ids are automatically updated.
                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1637272763825_199768_56156 (Explanation)
                Requirements Hierarchy - Population
                UML kind: uml:Package */
