                package 'L5 CubeSat Deployer Interface Rqts' {
                    doc /* Source XMI: _18_5_2_3880181_1543956528936_889838_63175
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600883445983_91995_63203
                    The design and development of the mission specific CubeSat must satisfy the Rqts for interfacing with a CubeSat Deployer.
                    The CubeSat team must document incorporation and satisfaction of the interface Rqts.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619533266740_930124_14430 (Explanation)
                    The design and development of the mission specific CubeSat must satisfy the requirements for interfacing with a CubeSat Deployer.
                    The CubeSat team must document incorporation and satisfaction of the interface requirements.
                    Typically, this would be a verification matrix that lists requirements with information such as id, description, source, verification method, verification status, and verification results.
                    Typically, verification matrices are implemented with a spreadsheet.
                    However, this verification information can be incorporated into attributes of a SysML requirement element and exported as a spreadsheet.
                    So … the mission-specific team needs to determine how to document and populate these interface requirements.  .
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619533266753_683834_14441 (Explanation)
                    These requirements use the DeployerInterfaceRequirement stereotype with the following properties:
                    Id   Name    Text
                    Source Document - CubeSat Deployer System interface specification
                    Source Paragraph
                    Satisfaction Status
                    Satisfied By - The satisfy relationship is used to assert that a model element corresponding to the design or implementation satisfies a particular requirement.
                    Verify Method -  Verification methods include inspection, analysis, demonstration, and test.
                    Verified By - The verify relationship is between a requirement and a test case or other model element that is used to verify the requirement is satisfied.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619533266760_332117_14452 (Explanation)
                    These requirements are to be populated based on / extracted from The CubeSat Deployer System interface specification.
                    For example:
                    Cal Poly CubeSat Design Specification  or
                    NanoRacks Interface Design Document
                    The interface requirement categories and Ids can modified as needed to be consistent with the interface specifications.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619533266766_631394_14463 (Explanation)
                    Having CubeSat Deployer Systems provide SysML models that contain the interface requirements would be very beneficial and will be pursued.
                    We have created SysML model of the Cal Poly CubeSat Design Specification, but it is not a Cal Poly product.
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1637954427474_621508_57510
                    CubeSat Deployer Interface Rqts - Population
                    UML kind: uml:Package */
