            package '2 - Technical Measures' {
                doc /* Source XMI: _18_5_2_3880181_1514819747685_920670_63005
                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600784866099_900680_62772
                Technical measures are an established set of measures based on the expectations and Rqts that are tracked and assessed to determine overall system effectiveness and stakeholder satisfaction.
                Stakeholders will likely describe their technical measures as text and captured in Technical Measure Specifications.
                Technical Measure Specifications have Traced To, Traced From, and Allocated To properties.
                They will communicate and negotiate these descriptions with engineers who will transform them into measures that can be tracked and assessed.
                Validation activities provide data to the technical measurement process that are used to assess how well the measures are either projected to meet, or are meeting, their stated value.
                UML kind: uml:Package */
                package '2.1 - Technical Measures - Specifications and Requirements - Population' {
                    doc /* Source XMI: _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510398_757978_55696
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_183490_55792
                    A Technical Measure provides a stakeholder insight into the definition and development of a technical solution.
                    Verification activities provide data to the technical measurement process that is used to assess how well the technical measure is either projected to meet, or is meeting, its stated value.
                    Common terms for these measures are MOEs, MOPs, and TPMs
                    MOEs are operational measures of success closely related to the achievement of the mission objective in the intended operational environment under a specified set of conditions.
                    MOPs are measures that characterize physical or functional attributes relating to system operation, measured or estimated under specified testing and/or operational environment conditions.
                    TPMs measure attributes of a system element to determine how well that element is satisfying, or expected to satisfy, a technical requirement.
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_102763_55793 (Explanation)
                    xxxx A Technical Measure is incorporated in to CubeSat Reference Model as a block value property based on the Technical Measure as specified by a stakeholder.
                    A stakeholder is going to most likely “describe” their Technical Measure in a document.  A stakeholder will communicate and negotiate their Technical Measure with the engineers and engineers will transform those descriptions into a value property.
                    These stakeholder specified TMs are captured in the Technical Measures Specification package.
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_626141_55794 (Explanation)
                    MOPs are measures that characterize physical or functional attributes relating to system operation, measured or estimated under specified testing and/or operational environment conditions
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_606473_55795
                    A Technical Measure provides a stakeholder insight into the definition and development of a technical solution.
                    Verification activities provide data to the technical measurement process that is used to assess how well the technical measure is either projected to meet, or is meeting, its stated value.
                    Common terms for these measures are:
                    - MOE - Measure of Effectiveness
                    - MOP - Measure of Performance
                    - TPM - Technical Performance Measure
                    - KPP - Key Performance Parameter
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_952148_55796 (Explanation)
                    xxxx Technical Measure Specifications have Traced To, Traced From, Allocated To properties.
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_409865_55797 (Explanation)
                    MOEs are operational measures of success closely related to the achievement of the mission objective in the intended operational environment under a specified set of conditions
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_546134_55798 (HowTo)
                    Double-click on a Technical Measure table and then click on Add New to add a new Technical Measure to the containment tree and to the table.
                    Right click the new element in the table then left click Select in Containment Tree to navigate to the new element.
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_726393_55799 (Explanation)
                    TPMs measure attributes of a system element to determine how well that element is satisfying, or expected to satisfy, a technical requirement
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636724536835_804872_56189 (Explanation)
                    xxxx Allocated To: Block (Enterprise, Segment, Subsystem), if a qualitative Technical Measure
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636724664792_513035_56195 (Explanation)
                    xxxx Traced From: Block (Enterprise, Segment, Subsystem) Threshold _Value, if a quantitative Technical Measure
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636724943040_947009_56249 (Explanation)
                    KPPs are measures that are critical and failure to meet threshold performance will result in reevaluation of a technical solution and with the possibility of project termination.
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1637271783478_475116_55706 (Explanation)
                    Technical Measures - Specifications and Requirements - Population
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1641150397420_260024_59013 (Explanation)
                    A Technical Measure is incorporated in to CubeSat System Reference Model as a block value property based on the Technical Measure as specified by a stakeholder
                    A stakeholder is going to most likely “describe” their Technical Measure in a document.  A stakeholder will communicate and negotiate their Technical Measure with the engineers and engineers will transform the description into a value property, and methods for calculating the value property.
                    The Technical Measures are captured in Technical Measures Specification packages and Technical Measurers Requirement packages.
                    Technical Measures Specification package diagrams are used to establish the relationships of Specifications, Methods, and Requirements.
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1641150688495_505749_59026 (Explanation)
                    The Technical Measures Methods document iis part of the model and can be edited within the model.
                    It can be created externally and copy/pasted into a  Technical Measure package diagram for populatiion into the containment tree.
                    The Methods can be be incorporated into the Constraint block Constraints and Parameters compartments.
                    Parametric diagrams show how the constraint properties are connected.
                    UML kind: uml:Package */
                    package '2.1.1 MOE' {
                        doc /* Source XMI: _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510398_734036_55697
                        Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510635_692691_55833
                        Repository for MOEs
                        UML kind: uml:Package */
                        package '2.1.1.1 MOE Specifications' {
                            doc /* Source XMI: _19_0_2_3880181_1639417985290_868805_56838
                            Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1640885278249_582300_57859
                            MoeA Methods.docx
                            Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1640890851803_36409_58290
                            MoeB Methods.docx
                            UML kind: uml:Package */
                            part def 'MoeA Specification' {
                                @OfficialCSRMProfile::'Technical Measures Profile'::'moeSpecification';
                                doc /* Source XMI: _19_0_2_3880181_1636387510572_262637_55801
                                Stereotype moeSpecification: summary=The system shall exhibit the property "MOE Name" that has a minimum of x and maximum of y,
                                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1641238341956_841688_59222
                                Technical measure description
                                UML kind: uml:Class */
                            }
                            dependency relationship_3 from OfficialCSRM::'Data'::'01 - CubeSat System Reference Model'::'2 - Technical Measures'::'2.1 - Technical Measures - Specifications and Requirements - Population'::'2.1.1 MOE'::'2.1.1.1 MOE Specifications'::'MoeA Specification' to OfficialCSRM::'Data'::'01 - CubeSat System Reference Model'::'2 - Technical Measures'::'2.1 - Technical Measures - Specifications and Requirements - Population'::'2.1.1 MOE'::'2.1.1.2 MOE Requirements'::'MoeA Requirement' {
