                    package '1.2.3 - Mission Stakeholders Requirements Relationships - Example' {
                        doc /* Source XMI: _18_5_2_3880181_1508899053594_724029_62629
                        Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600866306142_386403_63294
                        An example population of mission stakeholders - stakeholder concerns - mission objectives - mission needs - mission constraints -  mission Rqts.
                        Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1637703240911_208051_55600 (Explanation)
                        Mission Stakeholders - Requirements Relationships - Example
                        Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1639412813734_622430_56736 (Explanation)
                        The relationships betweeen elements are captured in the element specifications and containment tree.
                        Those relationships are displayed and maintained in diagrams and tables as shown below
                        UML kind: uml:Package */
                        package '1.2.3.1 - Stakeholders' {
                            doc /* Source XMI: _18_5_2_3880181_1524068060852_562509_66155
                            Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600979504067_339944_62960
                            Not part of the Foundational CSRM.  An illustration.
                            UML kind: uml:Package */
