            package '2 - Technical Measures' {
                doc /* Source XMI: _19_0_2_3880181_1612801652594_227615_62540
                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1638718750160_676640_56603 (Explanation)
                Technical Measures - Illustration
                UML kind: uml:Package */
                package '2.2 - Technical Measures - Specifications and Requirements - Illustration' {
                    doc /* Source XMI: _18_5_2_3880181_1523225290730_214038_65576
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600808302065_211818_63272
                    Not part of the Foundational CSRM.  An illustration of the role of value properties, constraint blocks, and parametrics in assessing technical measures.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619127788796_857234_621 (HowTo)
                    Double-click on the technical measure table and then click on Add New to add a new technical measure to the containment tree and to the table.
                    The new technical measure element is also added to the technical measure mapping matrix. .
                    Right click the new element in the table then left click Select in Containment Tree to navigate to the new element.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619128035356_39855_658 (Explanation)
                    Techncial Peformance Measures (TPMs) measure attributes of a system element to determine how well that element is satisfying, or expected to satisfy, a technical requirement
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619128035364_846453_680 (Explanation)
                    Measures of Performance (MOPs) are measures that characterize physical or functional attributes relating to system operation, measured or estimated under specified testing and/or operational environment conditions
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619128035376_95524_702 (Explanation)
                    Measure of Effectivenss (MOEs)  are operational measures of success closely related to the achievement of the mission objective in the intended operational environment under a specified set of conditions
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619128035420_626153_790 (Explanation)
                    Tecnical Measures - Specificationa and Requirements - Illustration
                    Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1641230829129_461941_59184 (Explanation)
                    Key Performance Parameters (KPPs) are measures that are critical and failure to meet threshold performance will result in reevaluation of a technical solution and with the possibility of project termination.
                    UML kind: uml:Package */
                    package 'Technical Measures Requirements ' {
                        doc /* Source XMI: _19_0_2_3880181_1638560756988_480993_56983
                        UML kind: uml:Package */
                    }
