            package '8 - CSRM Population' {
                doc /* Source XMI: _18_5_2_3880181_1552247476525_922944_67947
                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1600787738958_955086_62993
                Package containing an illustration of the CSRM elements along with CSRM element population package diagrams.
                Comment _19_0_2_3880181_1657567678920_50130_58802 (Explanation)
                CSRM Elements, Examples and Illusrations
                UML kind: uml:Package */
                package '8.2 - CSRM Elements' {
                    doc /* Source XMI: _18_5_2_3880181_1550588335855_478944_65126
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094165_518699_13979 (Explanation, HowTo)
                    Select Architectural Element
                    Select Edit Compartments
                    Select Element Properties
                    Select Part
                    Move from Hidden to Selected
                    Select Architectural Element
                    Select Part property
                    Select Directed Composition
                    Drag to Part element
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094169_418561_13990 (HowTo)
                    Set font size
                    Select Element
                    Select Symbol Properties
                    Select Font
                    Select Ellipses
                    Select 14
                    Select Show Stereotypes
                    Select Text, or .....
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094178_559416_14012 (Explanation)
                    A Technical Measure Specification captures the descriptions of technical measures in textual form.  Stakeholders will likely describe their technical measures as text.
                    They will communicate and negotiate these descriptions with engineers who will transform them into measures that can be tracked and assessed
                    The Technical Measure is specified as a value property of an enterprise, segment or subsystem element..
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094183_177554_14023 (Explanation)
                    The CSRM is a logical model consisting of model elements and diagrams.  Shown below are CSRM elements and example element properties.
                    The Mission-specific CubeSat Model (MCM) is based on the CSRM.  The MCM provide the basis for design and development of the mission-specific CubeSat.
                    The mission team identifies the systems engineering methodology to be followed and then updates the MCM organization, elements, element properties, relationships, and diagrams as follows:
                    1) Determine if the CSRM elements are necessary and sufficient.  If not, modify accordingly.
                    2) Identify stakeholders and stakeholder terminology such as concerns, needs, objectives, and constraints, as they relate to establishing mission requirements.
                    3) Establish the relationships between use cases, technical measures, and space and ground segment and subsystems requirements.  These relationships can be exhibited in model artifacts such as requirement tables, requirement diagrams, and dependency matrices.
                    4) Identify the model artifacts that are needed such as for: stakeholder buy-off, internal and external design reviews, and design specifications.
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094191_12910_14034 (Explanation)
                    A Behavior can be specified by a Behavior description, a Use Case diagram, or an Activity diagram
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094194_234431_14045 (Explanation)
                    The validation process can be captured in a:
                    1) Validation Activity
                    element properties, or
                    2) Validation Activity Diagram, or
                    3) Validation Activity Word document
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094198_567447_14056 (HowTo)
                    Select CSRM Elements
                    Select Create Element
                    Select Element
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094202_198795_14067 (HowTo)
                    Select Properties
                    Select Element
                    Select Edit Compartments
                    Select Element Properties
                    Select form Hidden and move to Selected
                    Comment _19_0_3_2b0010b_1619532094205_702138_14078 (HowTo)
                    Populate element properties
                    Select element
                    Select specification
                    Select a property
                    Select "emptyt box" to reveal eipses
                    Select ellipses
                    and depending on the property enter text or use the search function to locate and populate relational element
                    UML kind: uml:Package */
